---
/* The mark, docked from the first frame.

   The scroll intro (anaglyph meet → rise → monogram) is retired: the page
   opens with its end state — the M-squared monogram, the signature's own
   opening M stroke raised to 2ei, printed at the centre of the head of the
   page and held there. The M is cloned from the signature plate's first
   stroke at runtime so the mark and the autograph can never fork; the
   ±3.2-unit channel offsets are the docked fringe, baked in.

   Easter egg: pointing at the mark makes the pen finish the autograph.
   Both signature plates (the centerlines extracted by scripts/extract-sig.mjs,
   cyan Matt / red Mattei) are registered onto the mark's own M and drawn by
   dashoffset out of it, while the composition glides left to stay centred
   and the 2ei exponent gives way to the real tail. Leaving retracts the
   strokes back into the monogram. */
---

